# D13 integrated kernel audit — downstream-use (reverse dependency) probe

For each *key input* named by a D12 blocker-closure record, this probe builds the reverse
direct-use graph of all snapshot-internal declarations (`Poincare.*`, `Probe.*`, …) and
reports every declaration that transitively consumes the input in its **proof term or
definition body** (theorem bodies are unsealed with `value? true`).

This is the machine check behind the acceptance rule "no claimed blocker closure without a
constructor of that missing input and a downstream checked use": a constructor with zero
transitive consumers is reported as `USES=0` and cannot count as a closed blocker.

Emits `D13USE<TAB><input><TAB><transitive user count><TAB><sample users>` plus
`D13USEMISSING` for inputs that do not resolve.
-/
